# Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin puts every page in its own browsing
# context group, so a window it opens cannot reach back through window.opener
# and a site that opens it cannot keep a handle on it. Nothing here needs the
# opposite: /buy is a plain same-tab link to a redirect, every external link
# already carries rel="noopener", and the feedback form posts with fetch.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is deliberately NOT in this file. Astro emits it
# per page as a <meta> tag carrying a sha256 for each inline script, and those
# hashes change with the build, so a copy here would go stale on the next deploy
# and start refusing the site's own scripts.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# Everything under /_astro/ carries a content hash in its filename, so the URL
# changes whenever the bytes do. Without this, Workers Assets serves them with
# the same `max-age=0, must-revalidate` as the HTML, which puts a conditional
# request on the render-blocking stylesheet on *every* refresh — the round-trip
# that gave the buttons time to paint unstyled. See src/styles/tokens.css.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
